# Security policy

## Reporting a vulnerability

<!-- if PUBLIC -->
Please don't report a security vulnerability in a public issue, pull request or
discussion. Report it privately through GitHub instead: open the repository's Security tab
and choose "Report a vulnerability", or go to
https://github.com/{{REPOSITORY}}/security/advisories/new. The report goes privately to
the maintainers.
<!-- end PUBLIC -->
<!-- if PRIVATE -->
Please don't report a security vulnerability in an issue or a pull request. Report it to
the maintainers at {{CONDUCT_CONTACT}}.
<!-- end PRIVATE -->

A good report has:

- the version of {{PROJECT_NAME}}, and your operating system
- what an attacker controls, and what they gain
- the steps to reproduce it, as small as you can make them

## What counts

- Input that makes {{PROJECT_NAME}} run commands, read or change files, or reach systems it
  shouldn't.
- Secrets or personal data that leak into logs, output, files or other services.
- Ways around authentication or access control.
<!-- if AI_APP -->
- Text that steers the language model into making {{PROJECT_NAME}} do something it
  shouldn't, or data sent to the model that should have stayed on the machine.
<!-- end AI_APP -->

## Supported versions

Security fixes go into {{SUPPORTED_VERSIONS}}.
